WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.669 --> 00:00:01.669
as we speak.

00:00:01.669 --> 00:00:03.190
And it may already have happened.

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:08.280
By the time you listen to today's show, the
House of Representatives is debating in advance

00:00:08.280 --> 00:00:12.860
of voting and they may have already voted
by the time you listen to this about the second

00:00:12.860 --> 00:00:14.630
impeachment of Donald Trump.

00:00:14.630 --> 00:00:19.560
Now, you all know if you watched the Monday's
show and or the Tuesday show, that I believe

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:25.910
impeachment should not be a political calculation,
but rather a responsibility, a duty that the

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:28.369
House of Representatives has questioned.

00:00:28.369 --> 00:00:30.840
One very simple flowchart.

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:33.980
Did the president do something worthy of impeachment?

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.050
If the answer is yes, then you impeach.

00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:40.989
There are no other considerations because
it is such an important responsibility placed

00:00:40.989 --> 00:00:42.319
on Congress.

00:00:42.319 --> 00:00:48.780
What is very interesting is that this will
not be merely a partizan impeachment in the

00:00:48.780 --> 00:00:49.780
House.

00:00:49.780 --> 00:00:55.469
We are hearing from more and more Republicans
that they are indeed going to vote to impeach.

00:00:55.469 --> 00:00:56.780
They may already have.

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:58.899
Depends on when you listen to this.

00:00:58.899 --> 00:01:05.460
Congressman John CatCo from New York was the
first Republican to say publicly he will vote

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:10.890
to impeach Donald Trump over his role in inciting
a violent mob to storm the Capitol.

00:01:10.890 --> 00:01:11.909
Last week.

00:01:11.909 --> 00:01:16.100
He said he will join Democrats today when
they vote to impeach Trump for willfully inciting

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:19.259
violence against the government of the United
States.

00:01:19.259 --> 00:01:24.590
We then heard from Liz Cheney from Wyoming,
Republican congresswoman and daughter of former

00:01:24.590 --> 00:01:26.119
Republican Vice President Dick Cheney.

00:01:26.119 --> 00:01:29.429
She will vote to impeach today.

00:01:29.429 --> 00:01:36.229
Then we heard from Republican Congressman
Adam Kinzinger that he will vote to impeach,

00:01:36.229 --> 00:01:43.119
saying that it can what Trump did essentially
cannot be ignored, period.

00:01:43.119 --> 00:01:47.079
And this is starting to get very, very interesting.

00:01:47.079 --> 00:01:53.179
We also heard from Republican Congressman
Fred Upton that he will vote to impeach Donald

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:59.319
Trump, and that puts the number of Republicans
that will be voting to impeach Trump at more

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:00.319
than zero.

00:02:00.319 --> 00:02:01.319
And that's what matters.

00:02:01.319 --> 00:02:03.799
Now, ultimately, we will get the full number.

00:02:03.799 --> 00:02:06.359
We I don't yet know what it is as of this
moment.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:11.430
The vote is likely happening or minutes from
taking place.

00:02:11.430 --> 00:02:16.060
But ultimately, the real questions are going
to be in the Senate.

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:18.180
And we are going to talk about that in a little
bit.

00:02:18.180 --> 00:02:21.909
I don't I don't want to get ahead of myself,
but there is going to be a real question as

00:02:21.909 --> 00:02:25.940
to whether any Republicans would be willing
to vote to convict in the Senate.

00:02:25.940 --> 00:02:28.110
And we will get to that.

00:02:28.110 --> 00:02:33.330
Now, how much praise do these Republicans
deserve in the House for voting to impeach?

00:02:33.330 --> 00:02:34.540
Very little.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:35.890
That's that's the reality.

00:02:35.890 --> 00:02:38.770
The dominoes are falling and that's good.

00:02:38.770 --> 00:02:40.080
Republicans are starting to jump ship.

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:41.080
Many of them.

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.940
Many are not, but many are.

00:02:42.940 --> 00:02:51.110
And to me, this mostly is opportunistic individuals
trying to save themselves.

00:02:51.110 --> 00:02:54.159
That being said, I still say keep them coming.

00:02:54.159 --> 00:02:58.590
I still think, again, people should just vote
based on what happened.

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:03.290
What happened is Donald Trump behaved in an
impeachable manner and thus any vote to impeach

00:03:03.290 --> 00:03:06.340
is the correct vote and that should be welcomed.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:10.490
But it's a lot easier to be the second person
to take a stand.

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.910
And second applies in a number of ways here.

00:03:12.910 --> 00:03:15.849
This is the second impeachment of Donald Trump.

00:03:15.849 --> 00:03:22.130
We have already seen some Republicans like
Mitt Romney and others distance from Donald

00:03:22.130 --> 00:03:23.130
Trump.

00:03:23.130 --> 00:03:29.760
And it's always easier when your participation
is going to get less and less attention and

00:03:29.760 --> 00:03:34.670
the second person to jump on board gets less
attention than the first and the tenth gets

00:03:34.670 --> 00:03:36.210
less attention than the second.

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:38.099
And that's the way it goes.

00:03:38.099 --> 00:03:40.250
And ultimately, many of these.

00:03:40.250 --> 00:03:46.290
Republicans are realizing there's simply nothing
to gain and everything to lose from continuing

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:49.590
to side with a seditious president.

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:54.580
I hate to be so cynical about this, but this
is Republicans doing exactly what we predict,

00:03:54.580 --> 00:03:57.069
that they're just doing it like a week sooner
than we expected.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:03.920
And what I mean by that is there was every
indication for over a year, certainly for

00:04:03.920 --> 00:04:04.920
months.

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:10.120
And you've heard me talk about it every indication
that once Trump is gone, the Republican Party,

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:16.359
both those who supported Trump and those who
supported him publicly but not privately,

00:04:16.359 --> 00:04:21.480
and those who started to distance from Trump
publicly at a relatively earlier stage, this

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:23.020
was always the plan.

00:04:23.020 --> 00:04:28.480
The plan was always when Trump is gone to
do a sort of on steroids version of what they

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:29.620
did with George W. Bush.

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:32.870
Remember, George W. Bush did not campaign
with John McCain in 2008.

00:04:32.870 --> 00:04:37.640
George W. Bush was unpopular and Republicans
made the calculation.

00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:41.720
It probably hurts John McCain to have George
W. Bush on the campaign trail.

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:47.740
This is like a steroids version of that where
you are going to see tons of Republicans go

00:04:47.740 --> 00:04:49.200
into pretending Trump.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:53.140
I barely even remember that and I certainly
wasn't with it.

00:04:53.140 --> 00:04:57.770
And going back to all of the things the Republican
Party has pretended to care about for a very

00:04:57.770 --> 00:05:03.700
long time, we've got to reduce the debt and
the deficit, religious freedom, lower taxes,

00:05:03.700 --> 00:05:10.610
cut business regulation, get in the way of
so-called government takeovers by Democrats.

00:05:10.610 --> 00:05:15.210
And sometime maybe they'll call them communists
and socialists, et cetera, et cetera.

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:18.150
So this is not a surprise at all.

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:23.610
It's simply happening a week to two weeks
before Trump leaves office.

00:05:23.610 --> 00:05:26.410
We were more leaning in the direction that
it would happen.

00:05:26.410 --> 00:05:28.430
Once Trump is actually gone.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.430
That's it.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:30.900
And they deserve no praise.

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:35.310
They don't deserve to have their reputations
rehabilitated.

00:05:35.310 --> 00:05:40.410
But to the extent that it's correct for them
to vote to impeach, I'm with it.

00:05:40.410 --> 00:05:45.070
And after the break, we are going to talk
about what's happening in the Senate, including

00:05:45.070 --> 00:05:51.050
multiple reports that Mitch McConnell is pleased
with Donald Trump being impeached a second

00:05:51.050 --> 00:05:52.050
time.

00:05:52.050 --> 00:05:55.870
But what does that mean when Mitch McConnell
says that the devil is certainly in the details?

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:57.720
So we'll have more after the break.

00:05:57.720 --> 00:06:17.080
And also on our Instagram, which you can find
at David Pakman, The David Pakman Show at

00:06:17.080 --> 00:07:18.600
David Pakman Dotcom.

